description:
Every successful `topUp` or dispatcher-inflow `_syncBudget` performs the reset branch: `windowEnd = now + windowDuration`, `rewardRate = rewardBudget / windowDuration`. If the inflow is large (owner top-up, or a period of accumulated mint-debt being drained), the new rate is strictly higher than pre-call. The reset happens AFTER `_updatePool` settles pre-call accrual, so the higher rate applies only to time post-reset. An MEV searcher who observes the top-up in the mempool can:

1. Front-run with `stake(X)`;
2. Let the top-up land;
3. Hold briefly to accumulate emission at the bumped rate;
4. Back-run with `unstake(X)` + `claim()`.

There is no minimum stake duration. With `stakedToken` being the BalancerPooler ERC1155, a searcher with access to any amount of the NFT can sandwich every owner top-up. The `ownerOrNotGriefed` modifier explicitly permits rate increases, so the sandwich surface is 'by design' under the current modifier spec.
